  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 101 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nAs we remain under the midlevel ridge, high pressure will shift \neastward over the Ohio River Valley by midweek. This will bring us \nmild but pleasant weather for mid-November, with highs in the 50s \nand lows rising from the 30s to the 40s. \n\nModel signals suggest the potential for precipitation late next week \nas waves translate through an upper level trough over the Rockies \nand eject into the central CONUS. While there is uncertainty in \nwhere and when these systems impact the area, this may be an area to \nwatch as we head into the next week.",
